<title>JORDAN: Jordan dinar overnight rates rise to 1.63 percent.</title>
<headline>Jordan dinar overnight rates rise to 1.63 percent.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The weighted average overnight interbank rate of the Jordanian dinar rose fractionally to 1.63 percent on Tuesday from 1.61 percent on Monday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>It said three banks traded in 20 reported transactions worth 41.8 million dinars ($60.0 million).</p>
<p>$1 = 0.709 dinars</p>
<p>-- Amman newsroom +962 6 623 776</p>
